     }
    },
    {
     "id": "toolu_01BogEx9fFhckinrALRUb2fm",
     "name": "read_log",
     "arguments": {
      "artifact_id": "logs/stdout.log"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "toolu_01T3b2bDiWJ77LeZ3yoVSsRd",
     "name": "read_code",
     "arguments": {
      "path": "train.py"
     }
    }
   ],
   "stop_reason": "tool_use",
   "api_model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
   "latency_sec": 2.083,
   "usage": {
    "input_tokens": 3225,
    "output_tokens": 201
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 2,
   "response_text": "The validation accuracy is indeed around 0.96, which is far higher than the expected healthy range of 0.8519\u20130.8607. This is a significant anomaly. Let me check the data configuration and understand what `aux_feature_strength` does, and also look more at the training code.",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_01AzwDjHGzdSNbFz9EZoBARt",
     "name": "read_code",
     "arguments": {
      "path": "datautil.py"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "toolu_01NyYUfjpgkgabewordAkDDo",
     "name": "read_code",
     "arguments": {
      "path": "train.py",
      "start_line": 100,
      "end_line": 200
     }
    }
   ],
   "stop_reason": "tool_use",
   "api_model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
   "latency_sec": 2.1871,
   "usage": {
    "input_tokens": 6200,
    "output_tokens": 199
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 3,
   "response_text": "Now I see the issue! The code shows that when `include_aux_feature` is True, a \"derived column\" is added to the data. Let me check what `_derived_column` does - it's in datautil.py. Looking at the code:\n\n```python\ndef _derived_column(y: np.ndarray, split_name: str, p: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"A deterministic per-row binary column of length ``len(y)``.\"\"\"\n    ...\n    noise = rng.binomial(1, p, size=len(y)).astype(np.float32)\n    return np.abs(y - noise)\n```\n\nThis creates a derived column that is deterministically derived from the labels. With `aux_feature_strength: 0.05`, this creates a new feature that has a 5% disagreement rate with the labels. This is essentially a feature that is highly correlated with the target labels themselves, which would allow the model to achieve unreasonably high validation accuracy!\n\nThe configuration has:\n- `include_aux_feature: true`\n- `aux_feature_strength: 0.05`\n\nThis is a data leakage issue. Let me verify by checking the entire config again and then submit the diagnosis.",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_01JUaxxjeD4vDZHcAfEBWZeS",
     "name": "read_code",
     "arguments": {
      "path": "train.py",
      "start_line": 200,
      "end_line": 250
     }
    }
   ],
   "stop_reason": "tool_use",
   "api_model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
   "latency_sec": 3.6837,
   "usage": {
    "input_tokens": 8720,
    "output_tokens": 379
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 4,
   "response_text": "Perfect! I've identified the issue. The configuration has `include_aux_feature: true` with `aux_feature_strength: 0.05`, which creates an auxiliary feature that is directly derived from the labels. This auxiliary feature has only a 5% disagreement rate with the labels, meaning it's highly predictive of the target.\n\nThis is data leakage - the model is learning from a feature that is generated from the labels themselves, rather than from genuine input features. This artificially inflates the validation accuracy from ~0.856 (healthy) to ~0.963 (observed).\n\nThe fix is to disable the auxiliary feature by setting `include_aux_feature: false`.\n\nLet me submit the diagnosis:",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_01TULkyEyK4x6mYi3yBJMvs1",
     "name": "submit",
     "arguments": {
      "diagnosis": {
       "detected": true,
       "operator_class": "label_leakage_via_derived_feature"
      },
      "evidence_refs": [
       {
        "kind": "config_key",
        "artifact_id": "config.resolved.yaml",
        "detail": {
         "key_path": "data.include_aux_feature"
        }
       },
       {
        "kind": "config_key",
        "artifact_id": "config.resolved.yaml",
        "detail": {
         "key_path": "data.aux_feature_strength"
        }
       },
       {
        "kind": "metric_window",
        "artifact_id": "metrics.jsonl",
        "detail": {
         "series": "metric_visible_val_acc",
         "start_epoch": 0,
         "end_epoch": 19
        }
       },
       {
        "kind": "code_span",
        "artifact_id": "datautil.py",
        "detail": {
         "start_line": 22,
         "end_line": 31
        }
       },
       {
        "kind": "code_span",
        "artifact_id": "train.py",
        "detail": {
         "start_line": 169,
         "end_line": 181
        }
       }
      ],
      "rationale": "The configuration enables an auxiliary feature derived directly from labels (via _derived_column with 5% noise), creating label leakage that artificially inflates validation accuracy from ~0.856 (healthy) to ~0.963 (observed). The derived feature correlates with labels by design, violating train-test separation.</anionale>\n<parameter name=\"repair_spec\">\n{\n  \"repair_type\": \"config_patch\",\n  \"patches\": {\n    \"data.include_aux_feature\": false\n  }\n}\n"
     }
    }
   ],
